          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I want to build muscle and start going to the gym. What should my workout plan look like for a beginner?"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n1": {
        "id": "n1",
        "parent": "n0",
        "children": [
          "n2"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m1",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787260.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Here is a 4-day split, which is the sweet spot for a beginner who can train four times a week:\n\nDay 1 - Upper (push): bench press, overhead press, dips\nDay 2 - Lower body: squats, Romanian deadlifts, leg extensions, calf raises\nDay 3 - Rest\nDay 4 - Upper (pull): rows, pull-ups, face pulls\nDay 5 - Lower body: deadlifts, walking lunges, leg curls\n\nThree sets of 8-12 reps, 90 seconds of rest between sets. Add weight or reps every week - progressive overload is the whole game."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n2": {
        "id": "n2",
        "parent": "n1",
        "children": [
          "n3"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m2",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787320.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "On day 2 you said leg extensions. Is that the same as a leg raise? I have been doing leg raises and my quads aren't sore."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n3": {
        "id": "n3",
        "parent": "n2",
        "children": [
          "n4"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m3",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787380.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "They are different exercises, and that is exactly why your quads are not sore.\n\nA leg extension is a seated quad isolation: you sit in the machine and straighten your knee against a pad. It targets the quadriceps.\n\nA leg raise is an abdominal exercise: you hang or lie down and lift your straight legs at the hip. It targets the lower abs and hip flexors, and barely touches the quads.\n\nYou have been training abs on your leg day. Swap the leg extension back in on Day 2, and keep leg raises as accessory core work if you like them."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n4": {
        "id": "n4",
        "parent": "n3",
        "children": [
          "n5"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m4",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787440.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Good catch. I'm doing all this because I want to trek in the Himalayas next year - does that change the plan?"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n5": {
        "id": "n5",
        "parent": "n4",
        "children": [
          "n6"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m5",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787500.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "It changes the emphasis quite a bit. Himalayan trekking is long days of loaded walking at altitude, so it rewards endurance and leg durability more than maximum strength.\n\nKeep the 4-day split as your base, but add one long weighted hike per week, building from 90 minutes towards four hours with a loaded pack. Prioritise step-ups, walking lunges and calf work, and add steady zone-2 cardio. Do not drop strength work entirely - strong legs are what protect your knees on long descents, which is where most trekkers actually get hurt."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n6": {
        "id": "n6",
        "parent": "n5",
        "children": [
          "n7"
        ],
        "message": {
          "id": "m6",
          "author": {
            "role": "user",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787560.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "How much protein should I eat daily? I weigh 75 kg."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      },
      "n7": {
        "id": "n7",
        "parent": "n6",
        "children": [],
        "message": {
          "id": "m7",
          "author": {
            "role": "assistant",
            "name": null,
            "metadata": {}
          },
          "create_time": 1740787620.0,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "For muscle building, aim for 1.6-2.2 grams of protein per kilogram of bodyweight. At 75 kg that is 120-165 grams daily. Good sources: chicken breast, eggs, Greek yogurt, lentils and whey powder."
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "metadata": {}
        }
      }
    },
